My name is Marco.

3
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:06,470
My name is Kathryn and it's the holiday season.

4
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:09,970
Today we have a lesson all about a special December holiday.

5
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:10,690
That's right.

6
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:21,190
We are getting close to Christmas and of course today we are going to talk about Christmas in the United States and some of the typical traditions that you see over there.

7
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:21,930
That's right.

8
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:26,470
So we're going to be looking at a family as they wait for Christmas morning to arrive.

9
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:29,930
If you don't know what that is, don't worry, you'll hear us talk about it in a moment.

10
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,510
But first let's listen to our dialogue.

11
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:39,550
What are you doing awake?

12
00:00:40,310 --> 00:00:41,250
I can't sleep.

13
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,770
But it's almost midnight.

14
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:43,870
Exactly.

15
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,190
I'm too excited for Christmas morning.

16
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:48,930
Also, I thought I heard Santa.

17
00:00:49,670 --> 00:00:50,170
Really?

18
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:51,910
How do you know it was Santa?

19
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:58,850
Well, I heard that naughty boys and girls get coal in their stockings so I thought I'd be nice and make Santa cookies.

20
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:01,050
I even left out some milk.

21
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:05,030
I heard someone in the kitchen eating the cookies so I came downstairs.

22
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:06,430
Hmm.

23
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:11,830
Well, I know that Santa won't come down the chimney with you hiding behind the tree spying on him.

24
00:01:12,190 --> 00:01:12,570
Really?

25
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:13,970
Really.

26
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:15,970
Let's go back upstairs and get back to bed.

27
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:18,070
That way we can let Santa do his job.

28
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:20,590
Then when you wake up, it will be Christmas already.

29
00:01:21,010 --> 00:01:21,390
Okay.

30
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,540
Hey, honey, is that you?

31
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:29,860
Don't eat all the cookies.

32
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,180
I want some too.

33
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:35,420
Alright, we're back.

34
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:38,700
So now let's take a look at some language on Language Takeaway.

35
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:42,560
Language Takeaway.

36
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:47,070
Okay, I just said it but here's that phrase again.

37
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:48,290
Christmas morning.

38
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:49,330
That's right.

39
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:54,550
So Christmas morning is December 25th in the morning, right?

40
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:55,760
That's right.

41
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,760
Okay.

42
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:04,280
Okay, so the tradition is that small children will wake up early and run downstairs and they will find Christmas presents under the Christmas tree.

43
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,930
And so this is the Christmas morning tradition.

44
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:10,830
Many countries, they celebrate Christmas on Christmas Eve, the 24th, right?

45
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:20,240
Alright, so Christmas Eve is December 24th, Christmas Day or if it's in the morning, Christmas morning is December 25th.

46
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:29,880
And as you said, kids come downstairs or go to where the Christmas tree is to look for their presents that Santa came and left for them.

47
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:30,880
That's right.

48
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:37,000
So the idea, the story is that Santa comes at night, late at night and brings presents for the children.

49
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,560
And when the children wake up, they see the presents but Santa has already gone.

50
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:48,220
So Santa is a man, he's kind of a mythical figure with a big white beard and a red outfit and a red hat.

51
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:49,920
Right.

52
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,310
So his name is Santa Claus or just Santa.

53
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:58,920
There are many, many different names for Santa in different cultures and different countries.

54
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:05,390
Yeah, some people like to call him Saint Nick or Saint Nicholas but most people will call him Santa in America.

55
00:03:05,610 --> 00:03:06,150
That's right.

56
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:12,510
So this is what happens or part of what happens during Christmas Eve and Christmas Day.

57
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:19,850
And usually also, boys and girls will find our stockings that will be filled with candy or small toys as well.

58
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,320
That's right.

59
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,010
Stockings are basically socks.

60
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:30,350
But these are special socks that you don't wear, you hang them and a lot of people like to put them on the fireplace.

61
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,870
They hang them from the fireplace.

62
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:34,330
And like you said, Marco, they're filled with sweets.

63
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:43,720
The story says that boys and girls who are nice get good things like sweets and toys and boys and girls who are naughty get coal.

64
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:44,720
Coal.

65
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:49,760
So that's that black material that we use to make a barbecue for example.

66
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:50,380
Yeah, exactly.

67
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,640
It's very dirty and it's not something you want in your stocking.

68
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:53,940
Okay.

69
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:54,560
That's right.

70
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,460
So that's what we get in our stockings.

71
00:03:56,940 --> 00:04:06,940
And now when the small boy and his father were talking, they were saying that he should go back to bed and not hide behind the tree.

72
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:11,360
So if they're in the living room or they're downstairs in the house, what tree do they have?

73
00:04:11,650 --> 00:04:14,150
We're not talking about a big real tree outside.

74
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:16,710
We're talking about the Christmas tree.

75
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:20,030
But you know, it's a long phrase, the Christmas tree.

76
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,800
We don't have to say it that way.

77
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,710
When we have a Christmas tree inside the house, we can just call it the tree.

78
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:25,530
Okay.

79
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:34,190
And the Christmas tree, as many of you may have seen already, is a pine tree usually and you put decorations on it and the presents go under it.

80
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:34,810
That's right.

81
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:41,550
So you might hear this phrase, there are presents under the tree or there are many nice presents under the tree.

82
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,640
That means there are lots of nice presents under the Christmas tree.

83
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:44,810
That's right.

84
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:50,270
And well, the kid wanted to stay behind the tree and spy on Santa Claus.

85
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,120
That's right.

86
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,800
So this is a verb, to spy.

87
00:04:53,800 --> 00:05:00,290
This means to watch someone but to watch them while they don't know that you're watching them.

88
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,290
So you're hiding but looking at someone else.

89
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:02,690
Right.

90
00:05:02,890 --> 00:05:03,270
You're spying.

91
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:07,770
This is where the noun comes, a spy like James Bond.

92
00:05:08,150 --> 00:05:09,370
James Bond spies.

93
00:05:10,050 --> 00:05:11,730
He is a very famous spy.

94
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:12,190
That's right.

95
00:05:12,290 --> 00:05:17,510
But in this case, the boy does not want Santa Claus to see him so he is spying on Santa Claus.

96
00:05:17,950 --> 00:05:18,390
All right.

97
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:19,450
Very good stuff.

