00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:40,040
So, Marco, there's another great phrase in here that we often use just around Christmas.

126
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,260
What is it that Santa Claus does?

127
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:50,260
Well, the way Santa Claus leaves presents for boys and girls is that he will come down the chimney.

128
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:57,140
We saw that when the dad said, well, Santa Claus won't come down the chimney if you're here hiding behind the tree.

129
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,560
All right.

130
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,040
So the chimney is part of the fireplace.

131
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:04,840
A fireplace is where you have a fire in your house to keep warm.

132
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,900
And the chimney is where the smoke goes to come outside.

133
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,720
But Santa Claus goes the other way.

134
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:13,240
He comes down the chimney from the roof into your house.

135
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:13,980
That's right.

136
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:15,320
And then he leaves the presents.

137
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:19,280
So the father said, all right, so, you know, stop spying on Santa.

138
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:23,000
Let's go back upstairs and get back to bed.

139
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:23,450
All right.

140
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,310
Get back to bed.

141
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,320
And this is a phrase that you're going to hear parents say a lot to their children.

142
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:32,230
So if the children are awake or walking around, you say, get back to bed.

143
00:07:32,230 --> 00:07:33,570
That means go back to sleep.

144
00:07:33,910 --> 00:07:34,830
Go back to sleep.

145
00:07:35,010 --> 00:07:35,350
That's right.

146
00:07:35,990 --> 00:07:42,250
And we want the kid to go back to sleep so we can let Santa do his job.

147
00:07:42,770 --> 00:07:43,250
All right.

148
